          ],
          "content": "Symmetry"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.12,
            0.447,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": "Let us explore more figures."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.15,
            0.835,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": "Can you draw a figure with radial arms that has a) exactly 5 angles of symmetry, b) 6 angles of symmetry? Also find the angles of symmetry in each case."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.219,
            0.833,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": "Hint: Use 5 radial arms for the first case. What should the angle between two adjacent radial arms be?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.271,
            0.836,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "Consider a figure with radial arms having exactly 7 angles of symmetry. What will be its smallest angle of symmetry? Is the number of degrees a whole number in this case? If not, express it as a mixed fraction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.366,
            0.76,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": "Let us find the angles of symmetry for other kinds of figures."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.395,
            0.309,
            0.417
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
